From efd9c1bca1c6bf79438b3b4d95457f44336eba76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:01:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: courier and origin-bound creates join the
 worker queue; move --pool repins any ready worker-first card

t_01a1d0571c2f07d6 (defect kanban-71e066475f): after every gateway flipped to kanban.placement.worker_queue (11-12
12:35Z), 8 cards created by 15:20Z still got placement_policy worker-first-v1, which reserves ONE worker and writes
runs_on [machine:worker-N]. All 8 were courier/origin-bound creates on the hub (7 with hub_admission.entry=courier):
courier_plan's deny called pool_route(queue=False), _origin_enrollment passed queue=False, and queue_decision
excluded origin_intent. abec81ec81 introduced the courier/origin-bound exclusion without a reason; no constraint
was found for it: runs_on is a Board placement field the hub (a Board primary) already writes for local creates,
the courier envelope stores create_task options (runs_on included) immutably, and origin binding is a notify
subscription independent of execution placement.

- courier_plan: a deny takes pool_route with the queue (pool:worker + capability:hub-write), worker-first only
  without a live label; it refuses only when neither is possible (it used to refuse whenever the hub had no
  worker_pools entry, even with a live queue label).
- _prior_landing: a replayed courier request rebuilds the queued runs_on, so a lost reply does not raise
  origin_creation_conflict.
- _origin_enrollment uses the queue like a local create; new _landing_placement applies a queued runs_on for
  courier and origin-bound creates (the tool applied marker runs_on only on the routed path).
- queue_decision no longer excludes origin_intent.
- kanban_worker_repin: move --pool of a ready worker-first card (started or not) is a Board repin to
  [pool:worker, *coordination labels]; the origin repin keeps its unstarted rule. The Board's repinWorker already
  accepts any valid labels for a ready, unleased card of its creator, so no Board change is needed. Scheduled
  cards stay refused (the Board requires ready); move them once they wake.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pool_queue.py, test_kanban_worker_repin.py): courier deny -> [pool:worker,
capability:hub-write] and replay; origin-bound tool create -> [pool:worker]; started worker-first card moves --pool;
explicit pins, hub-pinned denies and no-queue-no-pool denies still refuse/win. 12 red on 59acb8fc0f, green on head;
16 mutants of the added conditions: 15 killed, 1 equivalent (_pool_target's `extra - {label}`: required_labels
never returns the pool label; kept for parity with pool_route).
